==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|bodies}}, plural of {{m|en|body||upper part of a dress}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɒdɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈbɑːdɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|bodices}}

# {{context|fashion|lang=en}} A [[sleeveless]] [[shirt]] for [[women]], [[sometimes]] [[provide]]d [[detachable]] [[sleeves]].
# {{context|fashion|lang=en}} {{altname|blouse|lang=en|nodot=a}}: [[any]] [[shirt]] for [[women]], ''[[particularly]]'' the [[upper]] [[part]] of a [[two-piece]] [[dress]] or in [[European]] [[folk]] [[costume]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1956|author=[[w:Delano Ames|Delano Ames]]|title=Crime out of Mind|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5915292W|passage=On the cover of the leaflet advertising the Alpenrose Gasthof in Zirl am Gurgl […] there is a decorative picture of a young woman. She is wearing Tyrolese costume: the low-cut white '''bodice''' with cross-laced velvet waistcoat, the floral apron and dirndl skirt.}}
# {{context|fashion|lang=en}} The [[upper]] [[portion]] of a [[women]]'s [[one-piece]] [[dress]], [[equivalent]] to a [[shirt]].
# {{context|fashion|lang=en}} {{altname|underbodice|lang=en|nodot=a}}: an [[undershirt]] for [[women]], ''[[particularly]]'' {{context|archaic|lang=en}} a [[corset]] or [[other]] [[undershirt]] [[stiffen]]ed with [[whalebone]].

